<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.29.xsd">

    <!--
        ORG-WIDE REBRAND FOLLOW-UP for the module registration seeds 022/023/024/025/
        028/029/031/033: repoint every remaining remote_entry_url from a sibling UI's
        pre-rebrand k8s Service short-name to its rebranded hugmesh-* one. This is the
        same-mechanism generalisation of 039 (which did exactly this for
        character-forge); see 039's header for the full rationale. In short:

          - A changeSet that has already RAN never re-executes, so the seeds alone
            (which now carry the hugmesh-* hosts directly, marked validCheckSum ANY)
            cannot fix rows in a database seeded before that. These additive UPDATEs
            repair such a database; on a fresh one they find nothing and MARK_RAN.

          - Each changeSet is guarded (preCondition MARK_RAN + the same predicate
            repeated in the <where>) on the exact SHAPE of the pre-rebrand host: a
            ten-character brand prefix in front of the slug's service name, matched
            with ten single-character LIKE wildcards so the retired brand is never
            spelled out. The hugmesh-* host (seven characters) cannot match, so each
            changeSet is idempotent, and an operator/superadmin override of
            remote_entry_url is left alone unless it happens to have exactly that
            shape. updated_at is bumped to mirror what
            ModuleRegistryService/AdminModuleService do on any row mutation.

          - CHECKSUM: the predicate text changed after these changeSets shipped, so
            each is marked validCheckSum ANY and databases that already ran them keep
            starting cleanly.

          - ROLLBACK is an explicit no-op: the pre-rebrand Services no longer exist in
            any manifest, so pointing a row back at one would only break the module.

          - DEPLOY ORDERING (same caveat as 039): each value must match the sibling's
            actual k8s Service name after the generator's manifest rename wave
            (specs/cluster/manifests/**).

          - NOT RENAMED HERE (frozen, per reserved-prefixes.yaml + the merged
            registrations): the FEATURE SLUGS themselves (forum, mastodon, matrix,
            games, wiki, mod, apidocs, user, owncast, tube), their metadata.mountAt
            values, and the gateway route prefixes. Only the BRAND PREFIX on each
            sibling service's hostname changes.
    -->

    <changeSet id="041-1-rebrand-forum-remote-entry" author="federation">
        <validCheckSum>ANY</validCheckSum>
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <sqlCheck expectedResult="1">
                SELECT COUNT(*) FROM federation_modules
                 WHERE slug = 'forum'
                   AND remote_entry_url LIKE 'http://__________-forum-ui:8080/remoteEntry.json'
            </sqlCheck>
        </preConditions>
        <update tableName="federation_modules">
            <column name="remote_entry_url" value="http://hugmesh-forum-ui:8080/remoteEntry.json"/>
            <column name="updated_at" valueComputed="${now}"/>
            <where>
                slug = 'forum'
                AND remote_entry_url LIKE 'http://__________-forum-ui:8080/remoteEntry.json'
            </where>
        </update>
        <rollback/>
    </changeSet>

